  "visualBrief": "Dated2013–2019 Harlem Apollo: four-bay glazed white terracotta front/five colossal pilasters, two square/transomed window tiers and fluted shield/meander spandrels, deep modillion cornice/open baluster parapet. Recessed western entrance/four doors under half-width projecting marquee with blue bands, pale display panels, warm soffit bulbs and two short-side APOLLO caps. Eastern glazed shop/yellow APOLLO fascia belongs to same frontage. Two-sided pale-yellow APOLLO blade with original geometric red letters/counters/neon strokes, open three-tier black steel trestle/V bracket. Exact native L-shaped stepped auditorium roof envelope; neighboring buildings/new Victoria spaces excluded.",
